{
  "_comment": "Network lab (ported from kvm-lab): pfSense router, Pi-hole DNS/DHCP and a Lubuntu client on the isolated segment lab-lan. Install with `vmctl lab install`, run with `vmctl lab up`. The topology lives once, in pfsense-lab.network_lab; the members point at it with gateway_vm. On plain QEMU the host reaches the lab through the router's WAN port forwards (hostfwd below + NAT rules in the rendered config.xml); after `vmctl export-libvirt` the segment is the libvirt network lab-lan with the host on 192.168.0.254.",
  "vms": {
    "pfsense-lab": {
      "name": "pfSense CE 2.7.2 (network lab router)",
      "meta": {
        "slug": "pfsense",
        "family": "bsd",
        "role": "router",
        "release_model": "stable"
      },
      "iso": "isos/pfSense-CE-2.7.2-RELEASE-amd64.iso",
      "disk": {
        "path": "artifacts/pfsense-lab/disk.qcow2",
        "size": "20G",
        "format": "qcow2",
        "interface": "virtio"
      },
      "firmware": {
        "type": "bios"
      },
      "machine": "pc",
      "memory_mb": 2048,
      "cpus": 2,
      "network": "user",
      "networks": [
        {
          "id": "wan",
          "type": "user",
          "ssh": true,
          "hostfwd": [
            {
              "host_port": 8080,
              "guest_port": 80
            },
            {
              "host_port": 8081,
              "guest_port": 8081
            },
            {
              "host_port": 2238,
              "guest_port": 2238
            },
            {
              "host_port": 2239,
              "guest_port": 2239
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "lan",
          "type": "segment",
          "name": "lab-lan"
        }
      ],
      "audio": false,
      "usb_tablet": false,
      "video": {
        "default": "std",
        "variants": {
          "std": [
            "-vga",
            "std",
            "-display",
            "gtk"
          ],
          "safe": [
            "-vga",
            "std",
            "-display",
            "gtk"
          ]
        }
      },
      "notes": "Unattended pfSense via bootstrap-pfsense: the offline CE 2.7.2 installer is scripted (bsdinstall, ZFS on vtbd0, BIOS) and the whole config.xml is rendered from network_lab. Netgate publishes no stable download URL: put the DVD ISO at isos/pfSense-CE-2.7.2-RELEASE-amd64.iso or point 'iso' at it in local.json. WAN = vtnet0 (slirp, DHCP), LAN = vtnet1 (segment lab-lan, 192.168.0.1). From the host: web GUI http://127.0.0.1:8080/ (WAN rules allow GUI + SSH from the WAN side), SSH 127.0.0.1:2237; 8081/2238/2239 are NAT forwards to Pi-hole web and to the members' SSH. Not a Linux guest: no ssh_provision post-install, the account below is created by the installer.",
      "ssh_provision": {
        "hostname": "firewall",
        "user": "lab",
        "ssh_host_port": 2237
      },
      "pfsense_config": {
        "username": "lab",
        "password": "lab",
        "timezone": "UTC"
      },
      "network_lab": {
        "role": "pfsense",
        "hostname": "firewall",
        "ip": "192.168.0.1",
        "lan": {
          "name": "lab-lan",
          "subnet": "192.168.0.0/24",
          "host_ip": "192.168.0.254",
          "bridge": "virbr-lab",
          "domain": "qlan"
        },
        "dhcp": {
          "enabled": true,
          "start": "192.168.0.150",
          "end": "192.168.0.199",
          "lease_hours": 24
        }
      }
    },
    "pihole-lab": {
      "name": "Pi-hole v6 on Ubuntu 22.04 (network lab DNS)",
      "meta": {
        "slug": "pihole",
        "family": "debian",
        "role": "server",
        "release_model": "lts"
      },
      "iso": "isos/ubuntu-22.04.5-live-server-amd64.iso",
      "iso_url": "https://releases.ubuntu.com/22.04.5/ubuntu-22.04.5-live-server-amd64.iso",
      "disk": {
        "path": "artifacts/pihole-lab/disk.qcow2",
        "size": "20G",
        "format": "qcow2",
        "interface": "virtio"
      },
      "firmware": {
        "type": "efi",
        "code": "/usr/share/OVMF/OVMF_CODE_4M.fd",
        "vars_template": "/usr/share/OVMF/OVMF_VARS_4M.fd",
        "vars_path": "artifacts/pihole-lab/OVMF_VARS.fd"
      },
      "machine": "q35",
      "memory_mb": 2048,
      "cpus": 2,
      "network": "user",
      "networks": [
        {
          "id": "install",
          "type": "user",
          "phase": "install"
        },
        {
          "id": "lan",
          "type": "segment",
          "name": "lab-lan",
          "phase": "runtime"
        }
      ],
      "audio": false,
      "usb_tablet": false,
      "video": {
        "default": "safe",
        "installer_order": [
          "std",
          "safe"
        ],
        "variants": {
          "std": [
            "-vga",
            "std",
            "-display",
            "gtk"
          ],
          "safe": [
            "-vga",
            "std",
            "-display",
            "gtk"
          ]
        }
      },
      "notes": "Installs with the Ubuntu autoinstall flow on a slirp NIC (SSH 2238), then the post-install hook of network_lab installs Pi-hole v6 unattended (pre-seeded pihole.toml: upstreams, local records, DHCP pool) and writes the static LAN address 192.168.0.10 for the next boot. At runtime the only NIC is on lab-lan: SSH and the web UI reach it through the router (127.0.0.1:2238 and http://127.0.0.1:8081/admin/). The cloud-init sudoers drop-in gives the user passwordless sudo: the network_lab post-install hook runs its setup script with sudo over SSH.",
      "autoinstall": {
        "hostname": "pi-hole",
        "username": "lab",
        "realname": "Lab User",
        "password_hash": "$6$labsalt0$POq.mGL6qhDmEnplwYiYiuKyYy.U8EuL0G.ROmcWjbMIHXpKeoKRB6MI2ObMDS3NHOQiB/R9E4pAiaNp5HKou/",
        "timezone": "UTC",
        "keyboard_layout": "us",
        "storage_layout": "direct",
        "install_ssh": true,
        "packages": [
          "curl",
          "ca-certificates",
          "dnsutils",
          "qemu-guest-agent"
        ]
      },
      "cloud_init": {
        "hostname": "pi-hole",
        "user": "lab",
        "write_files": [
          {
            "path": "/etc/sudoers.d/90-{{user}}-nopasswd",
            "permissions": "0440",
            "content": "{{user}} ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "ssh_provision": {
        "hostname": "pi-hole",
        "user": "lab",
        "ssh_host_port": 2238,
        "post_install_run": [
          "pihole version",
          "systemctl is-active pihole-FTL",
          "sudo cat /etc/netplan/01-vmctl-lab.yaml"
        ]
      },
      "network_lab": {
        "role": "pihole",
        "gateway_vm": "pfsense-lab",
        "hostname": "pi-hole",
        "ip": "192.168.0.10",
        "web_host_port": 8081,
        "password": "lab",
        "upstream_dns": [
          "208.67.222.222",
          "208.67.220.220"
        ],
        "hosts": [],
        "cnames": [
          "pfsense.qlan,firewall.qlan"
        ],
        "adlists": [
          "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/StevenBlack/hosts/master/hosts"
        ]
      }
    },
    "lubuntu22-lab": {
      "name": "Lubuntu 22.04 (network lab client)",
      "meta": {
        "slug": "lubuntu",
        "family": "debian",
        "role": "desktop",
        "release_model": "lts"
      },
      "iso": "isos/ubuntu-22.04.5-live-server-amd64.iso",
      "iso_url": "https://releases.ubuntu.com/22.04.5/ubuntu-22.04.5-live-server-amd64.iso",
      "disk": {
        "path": "artifacts/lubuntu22-lab/disk.qcow2",
        "size": "30G",
        "format": "qcow2",
        "interface": "virtio"
      },
      "firmware": {
        "type": "efi",
        "code": "/usr/share/OVMF/OVMF_CODE_4M.fd",
        "vars_template": "/usr/share/OVMF/OVMF_VARS_4M.fd",
        "vars_path": "artifacts/lubuntu22-lab/OVMF_VARS.fd"
      },
      "machine": "q35",
      "memory_mb": 4096,
      "cpus": 2,
      "network": "user",
      "networks": [
        {
          "id": "install",
          "type": "user",
          "phase": "install"
        },
        {
          "id": "lan",
          "type": "segment",
          "name": "lab-lan",
          "phase": "runtime"
        }
      ],
      "audio": true,
      "usb_tablet": true,
      "clipboard": true,
      "shared_dir": {
        "source": "shared",
        "tag": "shared"
      },
      "video": {
        "default": "std",
        "installer_order": [
          "std",
          "safe"
        ],
        "variants": {
          "std": [
            "-device",
            "qxl-vga",
            "-display",
            "gtk"
          ],
          "safe": [
            "-vga",
            "std",
            "-display",
            "gtk"
          ]
        }
      },
      "notes": "Ubuntu Server 22.04.5 autoinstall + lubuntu-desktop with SDDM autologin (the lab client of kvm-lab, on plain QEMU). Installs and provisions on a slirp NIC (SSH 2239); the network_lab hook writes the static LAN address 192.168.0.100 (gateway 192.168.0.1, DNS 192.168.0.10) and disables systemd-networkd-wait-online, otherwise every boot stalls 120 s once the renderer is NetworkManager. At runtime SSH goes through the router: 127.0.0.1:2239. The host folder ./shared lands on the desktop via virtiofs. The cloud-init sudoers drop-in gives the user passwordless sudo: the network_lab post-install hook runs its setup script with sudo over SSH.",
      "autoinstall": {
        "hostname": "lubuntu",
        "username": "lab",
        "realname": "Lab User",
        "password_hash": "$6$labsalt0$POq.mGL6qhDmEnplwYiYiuKyYy.U8EuL0G.ROmcWjbMIHXpKeoKRB6MI2ObMDS3NHOQiB/R9E4pAiaNp5HKou/",
        "timezone": "UTC",
        "keyboard_layout": "us",
        "storage_layout": "direct",
        "install_ssh": true,
        "packages": [
          "lubuntu-desktop",
          "spice-vdagent",
          "qemu-guest-agent",
          "arc-theme"
        ]
      },
      "cloud_init": {
        "hostname": "lubuntu",
        "user": "lab",
        "write_files": [
          {
            "path": "/etc/sudoers.d/90-{{user}}-nopasswd",
            "permissions": "0440",
            "content": "{{user}} ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD:ALL\n"
          },
          {
            "path": "/etc/sddm.conf.d/vmctl-autologin.conf",
            "permissions": "0644",
            "content": "[Autologin]\nUser={{user}}\nSession=Lubuntu\n"
          }
        ],
        "runcmd": [
          "systemctl set-default graphical.target",
          "systemctl enable sddm"
        ]
      },
      "ssh_provision": {
        "hostname": "lubuntu",
        "user": "lab",
        "ssh_host_port": 2239,
        "post_install_run": [
          "systemctl get-default",
          "sudo cat /etc/netplan/01-vmctl-lab.yaml",
          "systemctl is-enabled systemd-networkd-wait-online.service || true"
        ]
      },
      "network_lab": {
        "role": "client",
        "gateway_vm": "pfsense-lab",
        "hostname": "lubuntu",
        "ip": "192.168.0.100"
      }
    }
  }
